{"name":"Bengal","hex":"#cc974d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bengal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A geographic region in the northeast of South Asia today divided between Bangladesh and India (particularly the state of West Bengal)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A short-haired domestic cat of a particular breed that originated in the United States.","A player on the team The Cincinnati Bengals."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bengal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bengal","blocks":[{"text":"Bengal is a geographical, ethnolinguistic, historically geopolitical region in South Asia north of the Bay of Bengal. It is politically divided between the sovereign state of Bangladesh, the Indian state of West Bengal, Tripura, Barak Valley, parts of Assam and Jharkhand and Maungdaw District of the Rakhine State of Myanmar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Free_State_of_Bengal.svg/330px-Free_State_of_Bengal.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bengal","wikidata":"Q80338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bengali_dialects.png/500px-Bengali_dialects.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bengali_dialects.png/1280px-Bengali_dialects.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bengali_dialects.png/500px-Bengali_dialects.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABengali_dialects.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Geographic_distribution_of_Bengali_language.png/500px-Geographic_distribution_of_Bengali_language.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam